labwc-ospite — OUR labwc, only to host the nested KWin >= 6.5
=============================================================

Why: KWin >= 6.5 draws a black single pixel as the root of its window and puts the content in subsurfaces;
wlroots never reports that root as "presented", so KWin gives its clients a clock at 0 and Firefox thinks
its window is covered and stops painting.  The fix is a few lines in wlroots (types/scene/surface.c,
frame_done).  So that we do not depend on the distribution's wlroots (which lacks the fix), the package
carries labwc 0.9.3 with wlroots 0.19.2 + the patch, linked STATICALLY, as /usr/libexec/remotix/labwc.
src/kwin.c starts it only for KDE (make LABWC=...); XFCE and LXQt use the distribution's labwc.

Files
  VERSIONS     labwc and wlroots, pinned, with sha256 and URL
  fetch.sh     fetch.sh DIR            downloads the two tarballs into DIR and verifies them (sha256 of VERSIONS)
  build.sh     build.sh SRCDIR DESTDIR extracts, patches, builds with meson, installs DESTDIR/usr/libexec/remotix/labwc;
               fails if the binary links any libwlroots
  wlroots-0.19.2-remotix-presented-root.patch   our patch (MIT, like wlroots)

Build: the compiler flags come from the environment (dpkg-buildflags in debian/rules: hardening,
-ffile-prefix-map for a reproducible build).  Build packages (Ubuntu 26.04): build-essential meson patch
hwdata wayland-protocols libegl-dev libgles-dev libinput-dev libpixman-1-dev libseat-dev libudev-dev
libdisplay-info-dev libxml2-dev libcairo2-dev libpango1.0-dev libpng-dev libdrm-dev libgbm-dev
libglib2.0-dev libxkbcommon-dev libwayland-dev pkg-config curl.
  fetch.sh /some/dir && build.sh /some/dir /some/dest

Only for Ubuntu 26.04 (Kubuntu).  Licences: labwc GPL-2.0 (this archive is its corresponding source,
published with every release), wlroots MIT (THIRD-PARTY-LICENSES).
